IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wp45-nouns`
IMPORT `wp45-cross-references`

-- Row il-45. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the six sound references kept beside the defects, the date pair, and the date function.
-- Each control is a citation whose target exists and says what the citing words need; the first assertion of each pair shows that the two descriptions are the same kind,
-- the second that limb (a) does not hold, so the citation is not counted as a defect. Expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in wp45-cross-references.l4.

§ `Tests of the controls`

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: C1, section 2(b) to section 2 of the Cash Law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`both limbs hold` (`reference: C1, section 2(b) to section 2 of the Cash Law`))

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: C1, section 2(b) to section 4 of the Cash Law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`both limbs hold` (`reference: C1, section 2(b) to section 4 of the Cash Law`))

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: C3, section 25B to section 61 of the Penal Law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`both limbs hold` (`reference: C3, section 25B to section 61 of the Penal Law`))

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: C4, section 19(a) to section 182 of the 1995 version`)
#ASSERT NOT (`both limbs hold` (`reference: C4, section 19(a) to section 182 of the 1995 version`))

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: C6, section 1 (provident fund) to section 14 of the Severance Pay Law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`both limbs hold` (`reference: C6, section 1 (provident fund) to section 14 of the Severance Pay Law`))

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: C2, section 1 (postal bank) to section 88YA of the Postal Law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`both limbs hold` (`reference: C2, section 1 (postal bank) to section 88YA of the Postal Law`))

-- C5: 21 Tevet 5787 and 31 December 2026 are the same day (converted outside L4, see the references module).
#ASSERT `the Hebrew words and the printed date name the same day` (`commencement: Amendment 11 begins on 21 Tevet 5787`)

-- The date function. A day before the consolidation of 4 December 2025 is not answered (when section 73 of the Economic Plan Law began to apply was not read), so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the words naming the postal company are still in the Law on` (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the words naming the postal company are still in the Law on` (Date 3 12 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- From that day the consolidation already prints the replaced words, so no (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY).
#ASSERT `the words naming the postal company are still in the Law on` (Date 4 12 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the words naming the postal company are still in the Law on` (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
